# CARRIED OFF COSTS PLACE (mechanics improvement 4a; Survival.leave_bag). A
# lineman is struck at its round, takes hold, and a player who does not pull
# free is carried off. They wake far away with what was in the hand, told in
# words where their things are; the survey marks the place with an X lettered
# "your things"; and at the place the heap stands under the player's own pale
# rag on a stick, found by eye from well off. `use` takes it all back.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/bag_heap.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 --give=knife:1,driftwood:6,stone:4 --held=knife
coast calm
zoom 8
wait 0.6
spawn lineman
try 3
  walkto part 3
  tap swing
  await tell 8
end
await grip 6
shot 01-held-and-not-pulling-free with grip,mob:lineman
await skipped 12
wait 0.6
shot 02-woken-far-off-the-goal-says-where-your-things-are
tap map
await app:map 3
wait 0.6
shot 03-the-survey-marks-your-things with app:map
tap map
await app:none 3
near bag
wait 1.0
shot 04-your-things-under-your-own-rag with prop:cairn
zoom 16
wait 0.6
shot 05-found-by-eye-from-well-off with prop:cairn
hour 23
wait 0.6
shot 05b-and-after-dark-by-the-lens-in-the-knot with prop:cairn
zoom 8
press use 0.1
await took 3
wait 0.6
shot 06-taken-back
